  "name": "Real Estate Lead Capture & AI Response System",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "a55d3b4b-7410-43a0-b337-2ff30c466a7f",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## Real Estate Lead Capture & AI Response System\n\n### How it works\nThis workflow captures real estate leads from Typeform, validates that required contact information is present, and sanitizes the lead message. It uses Groq to generate a personalized reply, validates the AI draft, then stores the lead in Airtable and creates a Gmail draft while notifying the team in Slack. Separate fallback paths log incomplete submissions, AI-generation failures, and CRM-write failures to Google Sheets with Slack alerts.\n\n### Setup steps\n- Connect Typeform credentials and select the lead capture form that triggers the workflow.\n- Configure the email validation logic and map Typeform fields such as name, email, company, and message into downstream nodes.\n- Add the Groq API key to the HTTP Request node and confirm the chat completion model, prompt, and request body match the desired real estate response style.\n- Connect Airtable credentials and configure the base/table fields used for CRM lead upserts.\n- Connect Gmail, Slack, and Google Sheets credentials, then set the target draft mailbox, Slack channels, and spreadsheet tabs for successful leads and fallback logs.\n- Test each branch with complete leads, missing-email submissions, failed AI responses, and failed CRM writes to confirm alerts and logs work correctly.\n\n### Customization\nAdjust the Groq prompt, CRM fields, Slack message text, and Google Sheets columns to match the brokerage’s lead qualification process and follow-up tone."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b33fe094-3ca8-4014-9d51-7de3b7bff4a4",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        560,
        48
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 512,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Capture and validate lead\nCatches the property enquiry submitted via Typeform and checks that name and email are both present before anything else runs."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "883c8cb2-c2a0-4f65-86db-bdf335101e52",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        880,
        592
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 496,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Handle incomplete submissions\n\nIf name or email is missing, the enquiry is logged to a dedicated sheet for manual review and the agent is alerted on Slack. No lead is ever discarded."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "66671d2b-22e3-41f7-ba73-935c69a1b127",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1760,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 896,
        "height": 304,
        "content": "## Generate AI response\n\nThe enquiry message is sanitized (truncated at 500 characters) and sent to Groq (Llama 3.3 70B) for a short, personalized reply about the property. The draft is checked to make sure it isn't empty or a leftover placeholder before it's trusted."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fd889b66-1ccf-48dc-a333-47c8aedb6a82",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2464,
        592
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 496,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Handle AI failure\n\nIf the Groq draft fails validation, the lead is still saved to the CRM with a placeholder note, the team is alerted on Slack, and the enquiry is logged to a backup sheet for manual follow-up."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9380f5e8-3989-42f8-869b-911d83fc49cd",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3344,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 512,
        "height": 336,
        "content": "## Write and verify CRM\n\nThe lead is upserted into your CRM (Airtable), then the workflow reads back what was actually saved to confirm nothing was dropped or truncated before continuing."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "1e6edef4-fa53-4fc0-9561-71c67c6cec42",
      "name": "Sticky Note6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3792,
        784
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 672,
        "height": 304,
        "content": "## Log CRM failures\n\nIf the CRM upsert fails, or the write can't be verified, the lead is saved to a backup Google Sheet and the team is alerted on Slack so no enquiry is silently lost."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e6977fdf-4160-42f5-8729-a4964a829763",
      "name": "Sticky Note7",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4544,
        16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 800,
        "height": 304,
        "content": "## Finalize successful follow-up\n\nOnce the CRM write is verified, a ready-to-send reply is drafted in Gmail, the agent is notified on Slack with full enquiry context, and the lead plus draft are backed up to Google Sheets."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
